  "tagline": "The standard embedded JVM cache, with heap, off-heap and disk tiers and optional Terracotta clustering.",
  "description": "Ehcache is an embedded Java caching library and one of the most widely deployed JCache (JSR-107) implementations, used for Hibernate second-level caching and Spring's cache abstraction. Ehcache 3 stores entries across on-heap, off-heap and local disk tiers, and can be clustered through a Terracotta server. It is maintained by the Terracotta team, whose published artifacts now list IBM as the owning organisation. Releases are infrequent but ongoing (3.12.0 in April 2026). Use it when you want in-process caching in a JVM app, not a network cache.",
